  "notes": "You don’t need to be inside a football stadium to experience the match.\nThis SPL Reference measurement was taken at a distance from a stadium during a football match, capturing the crowd as part of the surrounding soundscape. From afar, thousands of individual voices merge into a continuous background presence, punctuated by moments when the crowd suddenly reacts as one.\nIt’s an interesting way to measure not just how loud a stadium is, but how far its acoustic footprint extends into the surrounding environment.\nEnvironment: Outdoor / urban\nSource: Football stadium and crowd, measured at a distance\nMeasurement type: Community / environmental noise",
